‎## Definition
‎**Fundamentals**: Core principles or foundations that everything else is built on.
‎If fundamentals are weak, the whole system becomes unstable.
‎
‎**Key Rule**: Fundamentals are what remain true even when tools, trends, or platforms change.
‎
‎## The 10 Technology Fundamentals
‎**Layered from base to top:**
‎
‎1. **Infrastructure** - The physical foundation
‎   Electricity, data centers, fiber, satellites, cell towers, devices
‎
‎2. **Networks** - How things connect
‎   Internet, mobile, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, payment networks
‎
‎3. **Protocols** - The agreed rules
‎   HTTP/HTTPS, TCP/IP, SMTP, Blockchain consensus
‎
‎4. **Compute** - Ability to process information
‎   CPUs, GPUs, Cloud, Edge
‎
‎5. **Data** - The raw material
‎   Photos, GPS, transactions, customer records
‎
‎6. **Software** - Instructions that tell hardware what to do
‎   OS, Apps, AI models, Websites
‎
‎7. **Security** - Protection of systems
‎   Encryption, Authentication, Backups, Access control
‎
‎8. **Distribution** - How technology reaches users
‎   App stores, Websites, APIs, CDNs
‎
‎9. **Economics** - Who pays, who owns, where value flows
‎   Who captures profit?
‎
‎10. **Governance** - Rules around technology
‎    Laws, Regulations, Standards, Privacy, Digital Identity
‎
‎**Each layer depends on the one beneath it.**
